From 7524bbf19d022667d449da3de62eaea704cdc277 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Torben Haack <t128n@ipv4.8shield.net>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 18:11:38 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] chore(web): draw Mermaid diagrams with Pele instead of
 Mermaid

Mermaid.js (1.6 MB gzip, 23 dependencies) is replaced by Pele (pele.run, 230 kB gzip, no dependencies), which draws the same Mermaid syntax. Pele renders synchronously and puts no <style> in the SVG (it references --pele-* variables instead), so the detour the old renderer needed for the production CSP -- the copy of the rules into a constructed style sheet and the second drawing it took -- is gone.

The colours of a diagram are mapped to the app colours in index.css, on the root of every picture, so a switch of the theme needs no second render; Mermaid drew each theme separately. The diagram is drawn at the body font, as before, and each picture gets a unique id prefix.

A failed drawing names the problem and, when there is one, the line and a picture of it; the long Expecting lists of Mermaid are gone.

The mermaid code fence, the languages and the diagram types are unchanged.
